cl exports the six ??_R0 type descriptors and cxx1's object does not name them, because cxx1 defines them file-local - the same deliberate choice the throw chain makes a few lines away in src/backend/Masm.cpp, and for the same measured reason: cl puts each in a COMDAT, MASM cannot say COMDAT, and a public copy collides with cl's (LNK2005). The objects are there and the runtime finds them; what it matches on is the name string inside the descriptor, not the symbol. Everything else agrees - the R1, R2, R3 and R4 records, the locator in front of every vftable, and the __RTDynamicCast call - and the case itself runs on this box and prints what clang prints.
